<title>GERMANY: Burson-Marsteller to promote Germany.</title>
<headline>Burson-Marsteller to promote Germany.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Public relations agency Burson-Marsteller has been tapped to help promote Germany's image as a top financial centre in a newly launched campaign, a senior Deutsche Bank official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Rolf Breuer, the designate head of Deutsche Bank, Germany's largest commercial bank which is active in spearheading the national effort, told a news conference that Burson-Marsteller would be creating advertising for the new campaign.</p>
<p>&quot;We will spend several hundred thousand marks on the campaign,&quot; which will be financed by groups participating in the effort to shore up Germany's reputation.</p>
<p>Officials at Burson-Marsteller were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
